==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|statut}}, from {{der|en|fro|statut}}, from {{der|en|LL.|statutum||a statute}}, neuter singular of {{der|en|la|statutus}}, past participle of {{m|la|statuō||I set up, establish}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈstætʃuːt/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# Written law, as laid down by the [[legislature]].
# {{rfv-sense|en}} {{lb|en|legal|common law}} Legislated rule of [[society]] which has been given the force of law by those it governs.

